findings.body:
**Template literals hide pragmas from the pragma check**

`pragmaAnchors` lists comments with a raw scan:

```ts
const scanner = ts.createScanner(ts.ScriptTarget.Latest, false, variant, text);
for (let kind = scanner.scan(); kind !== ts.SyntaxKind.EndOfFileToken; kind = scanner.scan()) {
```

https://github.com/AlexisBalayre/pupitre/blob/fa84a8c589d694c4b7547c68aa5625d08da6631c/tools/review/src/preflight.utils.ts#L97-L120

A bare `scan()` never gets the parser's `reScanTemplateToken` or `reScanSlashToken`. So the `}` that closes a `${…}` substitution comes back as `CloseBraceToken`, and the template's closing backtick starts a phantom template. That phantom runs to the next backtick in the file, across lines, and no comment inside it is ever returned as a comment token.

Repro:

```ts
// before
const url = `${base}/x`;
run();
const tag = `t`;
// after: only a pragma added
const url = `${base}/x`;
/* v8 ignore next */
run();
const tag = `t`;
```

- `pragmaAnchors` returns `[]` for both versions.
- The printer runs with `removeComments: true`, so its output is identical.
- `sameCodeIgnoringComments` therefore returns true, and `decideMode` returns `skip-comment-only`.

The same goes for `// @ts-ignore`, `// biome-ignore`, `/* c8 ignore start */` and `// eslint-disable`, which are the pragmas the PR says it always reviews. Templates with substitutions are common in this repo. For example, `src/core/merge-gate.service.ts:125` hides everything up to line 137. Regex literals such as `/'/` and JSX text also mis-tokenize, but only up to the end of their line.

If such a push is the last one before merge, an unreviewed coverage or type suppression lands on main behind a pending status. Later PR diffs won't show it, because by then it is in the base. No test puts a pragma after a template that has a substitution.

**Suggested fix:** take the comments from the parsed `SourceFile`, not a separate scan:

1. Walk the leaf tokens via `node.getChildren(sourceFile)`. Template parts, regexes and JSX text are real nodes there.
2. Before each leaf, including `EndOfFileToken`, collect `ts.getLeadingCommentRanges` and `ts.getTrailingCommentRanges` at the previous token's end.
3. Anchor each pragma by its leaf index and by whether a line break comes before it.

Also add tests with a pragma after `` `${x}` ``, after `/'/`, and after `` /`/ ``.
